{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1936","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1936","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1936\",\"parent_revision\":\"3e341d7b78e34eb3ea3275a35c36dc87a38b3b68\",\"root_revision\":\"e86388d04684ab297878e7ce9a31de3e9f0582734a2f1a079b672632cd1e809a\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaims verified against primary sources (2026-05-02):\\n\\n| Claim | Verdict | Source |\\n|-------|---------|--------|\\n| SKILL_TEMPLATE is a single constant with TODO placeholders | VERIFIED | init_skill.py lines 35-120 \u2014 single SKILL_TEMPLATE str confirmed |\\n| REQUIRED_ARGC = 4 is the current arg check | VERIFIED | init_skill.py line 33 |\\n| main() validates sys.argv[2] == '--path' | VERIFIED | init_skill.py line 338 |\\n| agent-templates.md documents archetype categories | REFUTED | File not found at plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/agent-templates.md \u2014 archetype guidance exists only inline in SKILL_TEMPLATE lines 50-72 |\\n| No templates/ directory under skill-creator | VERIFIED | No such path exists in filesystem |\\n| Four constants exist: SKILL_TEMPLATE, EXAMPLE_SCRIPT, EXAMPLE_REFERENCE, EXAMPLE_ASSET | VERIFIED | init_skill.py lines 35-203 \u2014 all four confirmed |\\n| TTY not available in Claude Code sessions | VERIFIED | .claude/rules/interactive-terminal-workarounds.md line 1 |\\n\\nKey finding: The archetype descriptions (workflow, task-based, reference/guidelines, capabilities-based) exist as guidance text inside SKILL_TEMPLATE itself (lines 50-72), marked for deletion by the author. They are not in a separate reference file.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: Domain-specific skill scaffolding templates for init_skill.py\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Add domain/template-aware scaffolding to init_skill.py so skill authors get a pre-shaped SKILL.md without manual editing.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent (add domain-specific template selection) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Item description confirmed against init_skill.py lines 1-373 \u2014 no --domain or --template flag present today\\n2. init_skill.py source constants (SKILL_TEMPLATE, EXAMPLE_SCRIPT, EXAMPLE_REFERENCE, EXAMPLE_ASSET) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read init_skill.py lines 35-203 \u2014 all four constants confirmed present\\n3. CLI interface: REQUIRED_ARGC = 4, sys.argv[2] == '--path' check | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: init_skill.py line 33 (REQUIRED_ARGC = 4), line 338 (sys.argv[2] != '--path') \u2014 confirmed\\n4. Interactive prompts not viable (no TTY in Claude Code sessions) | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: .claude/rules/interactive-terminal-workarounds.md line 1 \u2014 confirmed\\n5. Flag name (--domain vs --template) | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Item body contains both: Target State uses '--template', groomed sections use '--domain'. Human resolution required.\\n6. Domain/template list | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | Candidates (workflow, mcp-tool, reference-library, code-generator, agent-coordinator) derived from codebase patterns \u2014 not confirmed by human\\n7. agent-templates.md reference file | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: REFUTED | File not found at plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/agent-templates.md \u2014 prior groom claimed it documented archetype categories; source is actually inline in SKILL_TEMPLATE lines 50-72\\n8. templates/ directory | Snapshot: MISSING \u2192 Final: MISSING | No templates/ directory under skill-creator exists today\\n9. Backward compatibility | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Optional flag with default None preserves existing REQUIRED_ARGC = 4 invocation\\n\\nChanges from snapshot:\\n- condition 7 (agent-templates.md): AVAILABLE \u2192 REFUTED (file does not exist; archetype descriptions are inline in SKILL_TEMPLATE)\\n- condition 5 (flag name): still MISSING \u2014 item body contains conflicting values (--template in Target State, --domain in groomed sections)\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS (2 MISSING conditions require human input before implementation)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **domain-specific skill scaffolding templates for init_skill.py** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/coding-agents/raincast.md \u2014 pattern: Template-Driven Code Scaffolding (9 layout templates)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED (with two open questions for human)**\\n\\n| Input | Status | Source |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Add domain-specific template selection to init_skill.py |\\n| init_skill.py source (SKILL_TEMPLATE, EXAMPLE_SCRIPT, EXAMPLE_REFERENCE, EXAMPLE_ASSET constants) | AVAILABLE | init_skill.py lines 35-373 \u2014 all four constants confirmed |\\n| Step 4 as MANDATORY init step | AVAILABLE | SKILL.md lines 364-366 \u2014 CRITICAL annotation confirmed |\\n| CLI interface: init_skill.py skill-name --path path | AVAILABLE | init_skill.py REQUIRED_ARGC = 4 (line 33); main() validates sys.argv[2] == --path |\\n| Interactive prompts not viable | AVAILABLE | .claude/rules/interactive-terminal-workarounds.md line 1 \u2014 no TTY in Claude Code sessions |\\n| Which domain list | MISSING | Candidate list derived from repo patterns but not confirmed by human |\\n| CLI flag name (--domain vs --type vs --template) | MISSING | Flag name not specified; --domain is the most descriptive candidate |\\n| Backward compatibility | AVAILABLE | Optional --domain flag preserves existing invocation with no --domain arg |\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A \u2014 feature item. The absence is observable by running:\\n`uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/init_skill.py my-skill --path /tmp/test --template workflow`\\nCurrent output: exits 1, \\\"Usage: init_skill.py <skill-name> --path <path>\\\" (init_skill.py line 338 \u2014 sys.argv length check rejects extra args). Post-implementation: exits 0, creates /tmp/test/my-skill/SKILL.md with workflow-appropriate content.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 Blocks agent-driven skill creation efficiency. Every new skill created by /plugin-creator:skill-creator starts with a generic template requiring manual reshaping. With 19 skills in plugin-creator alone and active skill creation occurring regularly, the per-skill editing overhead compounds. P1 classification is appropriate.\\n\\nEffort: Medium \u2014 Core change is 50-100 lines in init_skill.py (add argparse argument + DOMAIN_TEMPLATES dict). Principal effort is authoring template content (one set per domain). Estimated 3-6 hours depending on domain count confirmed by human.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Efficient automated skill creation via /plugin-creator:skill-creator\\n- Bottleneck: Every new skill requires human or agent to delete generic scaffolding and write domain-appropriate structure from scratch\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Agents invoking init_skill.py during Step 4 skill creation receive a pre-shaped SKILL.md, reducing editing overhead\\n- Workflow skills get Mermaid flowchart stubs pre-inserted\\n- MCP-integration skills get FastMCP frontmatter and tool-listing stubs pre-inserted\\n- Reference-library skills get citation-first structure pre-inserted\\n- Backward compatible \u2014 no regression for existing callers omitting the flag\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen --domain workflow is passed to init_skill.py, the generated SKILL.md includes a Mermaid flowchart stub, domain-appropriate usage section, and workflow-specific example script rather than the current generic template.\\n\\nWhen --domain is omitted, behavior is identical to the current implementation \u2014 no regression.\\n\\nWhen an unrecognized domain name is passed, the command exits non-zero and lists valid domain names.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/init_skill.py my-skill --path /tmp/test` (no flag) exits 0 and produces byte-identical output to the current baseline (no regression).\\n2. `uv run ... my-skill --path /tmp/test --<flag> <name>` exits 0 for every registered domain/template name.\\n3. Same command with `--<flag> unknown-name` exits non-zero and lists valid names in the error message.\\n4. For each registered domain, `uvx skilllint@latest check /tmp/test/my-skill` exits 0 with no errors on the generated skill directory.\\n5. The generated SKILL.md for each domain contains domain-appropriate sections and zero structurally mismatched generic stubs.\\n6. `init_skill.py --help` output lists all available domain/template names.\\n7. SKILL.md Step 4 usage examples include at least one invocation with the new flag.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n1. Flag name conflict: the item body contains a discrepancy \u2014 the original Target State uses '--template', the 2026-04-26 groomed sections use '--domain'. Which flag name should be used in the implementation? (This affects AC wording and the SKILL.md examples.)\\n2. Which domains should be in the initial implementation? Candidate list from codebase patterns: workflow (step-based orchestration), mcp-tool (skills wrapping MCP servers), reference-library (pure documentation), code-generator (skills producing code artifacts), agent-coordinator (skills delegating to agents). Confirm, add, or remove.\\n3. Should an unrecognized flag value be a hard error (exit 1) or a warning that falls back to the generic template?\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Primary file | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/init_skill.py |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:skill-creator |\\n| Rule | .claude/rules/interactive-terminal-workarounds.md (TTY constraint \u2014 no interactive prompts) |\\n| Rule | .claude/rules/language-conventions.md (Python naming conventions) |\\n| Tool | uvx skilllint@latest check (validation of generated output) |\\n| Prior work | init_skill.py SKILL_TEMPLATE lines 50-72 \u2014 archetype descriptions exist inline here (workflow, task-based, reference/guidelines, capabilities-based) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None\\n- Blocks: Fully automated skill creation workflow in /plugin-creator:skill-creator (agents currently must hand-edit generic templates)\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 Core change: add optional argparse argument + DOMAIN_TEMPLATES dict to init_skill.py (currently 373 lines). Principal effort is authoring domain-specific template content (one SKILL_TEMPLATE variant per domain). Backward compatibility is low-risk. Estimated 3-6 hours for 3-5 domains with unit tests covering backward compatibility and error exit.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: ALIGNED\\n\\nThe item aligns with the plugin-creator plugin's mission of providing complete, high-quality skill scaffolding. The CLAUDE.md for plugin-creator explicitly documents that /skill-creator handles 'Create skills from scratch or templates' \u2014 domain-specific templates are a natural extension of that goal. The implementation pattern (template registry dict lookup) follows the same approach already used (SKILL_TEMPLATE constant selection). No divergence from stated design intent detected.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nSystems Inventory:\\n\\n| File | Change Type | Reason |\\n|------|-------------|--------|\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/init_skill.py | Modify | Add optional --<flag> argument, DOMAIN_TEMPLATES registry, relax arg count check for extra args |\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md | Modify | Update Step 4 usage examples to document new flag; add domain list reference |\\n| plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md | Modify (conditional) | Update Create New Skill section if it directly references init_skill.py argument format |\\n\\nNew files to create:\\n- Domain template constants (inline in init_skill.py OR as files under a new templates/ directory) \u2014 one SKILL_TEMPLATE variant per registered domain\\n\\nNo existing callers affected. Flag is additive; all current invocations without the flag continue to work via backward-compatible default.\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nTemplate registry pattern: define DOMAIN_TEMPLATES as a dict mapping domain name strings to replacement (SKILL_TEMPLATE, EXAMPLE_SCRIPT, EXAMPLE_REFERENCE, EXAMPLE_ASSET) tuples. When --domain is given, look up the tuple and use it; when absent, use the existing default constants. No other logic changes.\\n\\nThe --domain flag must be an optional argparse argument (with default None) to preserve backward compatibility. The existing REQUIRED_ARGC = 4 check must be relaxed to allow 6 arguments when --domain is present.\\n\\nTTY constraint: interactive prompts are not viable (no TTY in Claude Code sessions, per interactive-terminal-workarounds.md). The flag is the only viable mechanism for domain selection.\\n\\nCandidate domains (require human confirmation): workflow (step-based orchestration), mcp-tool (skills wrapping MCP servers), reference-library (pure documentation), code-generator (skills producing code artifacts), agent-coordinator (skills delegating to agents).\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nType: Feature\\nSubtype: CLI Argument Extension\\nPattern: Template Registry \u2014 existing scaffold function gains a domain lookup layer; existing callers unaffected when domain flag absent\\nScope: Single file change (init_skill.py) + documentation update (SKILL.md Step 4)\\nRisk: Low \u2014 additive change only; existing REQUIRED_ARGC path preserved for no-flag invocations\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent invoking init_skill.py during skill creation (Step 4), I want to pass a --domain flag to receive a template that is already shaped for my skill type \u2014 so I spend less time deleting generic example content and rewriting structural stubs from scratch.\\n\\nAs a human creating a new plugin skill, I want init_skill.py --domain workflow to scaffold a SKILL.md with a Mermaid workflow section already present, rather than getting a generic template I have to reshape.\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`init_skill.py` accepts a `--template <name>` flag selecting from a set of starter templates stored under `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/templates/`. Each template is a `.md.j2` (or `.md` with `{placeholder}` substitutions) file emitting a SKILL.md tailored to a concrete skill archetype. Initial templates cover the categories already documented in `agent-templates.md`: `workflow` (sequential procedures), `task-collection` (operations menu), `reference` (standards/specifications), `mcp-integration` (FastMCP-backed tool), and `doc-updater` (auto-updating external docs wrapper). When `--template` is omitted, behavior is unchanged (emits the existing generic skeleton \u2014 backward compatible).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/init_skill.py example-workflow --path /tmp/test-skills --template workflow`. The emitted `/tmp/test-skills/example-workflow/SKILL.md` contains a \\\"Workflow Decision Tree\\\" section, numbered Step headings, and zero `[TODO: Choose the structure that best fits this skill's purpose...]` blocks. Run `ls plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/templates/` and verify the directory contains template files for each documented archetype. Run `init_skill.py` without `--template` and confirm the generic SKILL_TEMPLATE output is byte-identical to the pre-change version.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nPattern extracted from research entry `./research/coding-agents/raincast.md` \u2014 Raincast's `src/lib/generation/templates/` provides 9 layout templates (chat, dashboard, editor, fileManager, dataTable, media, playground, utility, generic) where each template is a pure function emitting a complete React scaffold from app metadata. The local skill-creator already documents archetype categories but does not provide the executable scaffold-emitter analog.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/scripts/init_skill.py` emits a single SKILL_TEMPLATE constant with TODO placeholders regardless of the skill's intended purpose. Every new skill produced by `init_skill.py my-skill --path X` starts from the same skeleton with bracketed `[TODO: ...]` markers and no domain-aware scaffolding. The companion reference at `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/skill-creator/references/agent-templates.md` documents archetype categories (Standard Templates, Role-Based Contract Archetypes) but provides no executable scaffold-emitting code. Authors selecting a skill type (workflow-based, task-based, reference-based, MCP-integration, doc-updater) must hand-edit the skeleton each time. There is no `templates/` directory under the skill-creator skill that maps a chosen archetype to a concrete starter file.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"d1e9b4d4e18f04d0559aae60799993e2e01edbd338adbc37130a7aefc5faa1ab\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtYvSQ\"}"}